                    briefing_text_r1:       `The RFP is ambitious and vague, and contested inside NorthGrid: the CHRO sponsor wants <strong>behaviour change</strong>, the divisional MDs want <strong>technical reskilling</strong>, HR wants a <strong>reusable asset</strong>. These are three different programmes — trying to satisfy all three balloons the design to ~14 days per learner at an unfundable cost. Before any module, convert “leaders ready for a decarbonised business” into measurable, outcome-linked objectives, identify the <em>decision-economic buyer</em> who judges the renewal, and decide whether 120 leaders are one population or several. <em>Design the outcome before you design the agenda.</em>`,
